# interplay_lifetime_heap_discard_relist: A private heap across execs while the guest rewrites its pages between them. In-process a listed heap is paged once: the guest's new bytes stay unseen by an exec with flags 0; DiscardResources (63) makes the heap volatile and drops its transfer buffer, and the next prepare makes it non-volatile again and finds it host-valid, so it is not paged either; only invalidateHost (1) pages the new bytes in. In the service the heap is the guest pages: every read shows the latest bytes, and 63 detaches the backing, which the next listing attaches again.
